course: dictionary
lesson: 4747
title: One word, many uses: hose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hose is a long, soft tube that carries water. You can use one to water a garden, wash a car or fill a paddling pool. «Think of a garden hose bent round a flower bed» tells you a hose is soft and bendy.
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it. «Fire hose» means a big, strong hose that firefighters use. In «hose the mud off the bike», hose is a verb: it means to wash or spray something with water.
explain: Check the clues. If the sentence is about water, washing or fire, hose means the water tube or the spraying. If it is about old clothes, hose might mean stockings or tights.
fact: A hose is a long, soft tube that carries water.
fact: «Fire hose» means a big, strong hose that firefighters use.
fact: «Hose down» means to wash or spray something with a hose.
fact: Hose can also be a verb: you hose, it hoses, it hosed, it is hosing.
fact: Hose is an old word for stockings or tights.
exercise: «Think of a garden hose bent round a flower bed.» What does a garden hose carry? | *Water | Air for balloons | Sunlight | Sand
exercise: A firefighter shouts, «Grab the fire hose!» What kind of hose is it? | *A big, strong hose for putting out fires | A tube for drinking | A thin hose for garden flowers | A pair of tights
exercise: Ella says, «Hose the mud off the bike.» What does hose mean here? | *To wash or spray with water | To dig a hole | To wear as tights | To tie up tightly
test: «A fine spray from a garden hose, with your back to the Sun, can make a little rainbow.» What does hose mean here? | Sunshine | *A long, soft tube that carries water | A stocking | A big, strong fire tube
test: Dad says, «We hosed the dog down after the walk.» What does hose down mean? | *To wash or spray with water | To put on tights | To stretch out a rope | To dry with a towel
exam: In «A vacuum cleaner's fan pushes air out, so the air outside rushes in through the hose carrying dust», what clue tells you hose means a tube? | The word fan | *Rushes in through the hose carrying dust | The word vacuum | The word outside
